[00:12.75]1. At the start of the day, with the sun yet to rise,
[00:16.75]We are making our way
[00:18.75]with the sleep in our eyes, and we pray.
[00:24.67]We are there with a smile for the people we meet.
[00:28.92]Some may stop for a while,
[00:33.17]some pass by on the street, but we stay.
[00:37.41](Chorus)
[00:41.66]It’s the life that we choose;
[00:45.86]For Jehovah we live.
[00:50.06]And whatever he asks, we will do.
[00:58.84]In the work we endure,
[01:02.84]Whether sunshine or rain.
[01:06.84]It’s a way we can say ev’ry day: “I love you.”
[01:24.38]2. At the end of the day, with the sun sinking low,
[01:28.38]Feeling happy and tired,
[01:32.38]in our heart there’s a glow, and we pray.
[01:40.51]It’s a life that we love, always giving our best.
[01:44.76]And Jehovah we thank,
[01:49.01]for by him we are blessed ev’ry day.
[01:53.26](Chorus)
[01:57.51]It’s the life that we choose;
[02:01.51]For Jehovah we live.
[02:07.39]And whatever he asks, we will do.
[02:13.39]In the work we endure,
[02:18.39]Whether sunshine or rain.
[02:22.39]It’s a way we can say ev’ry day: “I love you.”